I'm not sure polypiling is necessarily the best way to do this, for
various reasons:

1) It might be a good way to get new spells, but not necessarily THE
spells I want. Even polypiling 12 spellbooks at a time (three stacks
of 4)
2) Spellbooks are heavy. To minimize the to-and-fro of getting to my
stash, I generally just drop them. Getting all your spellbooks in one
place takes *time*
3) Unicorns aren't THAT common that if you're playing quickly you will
have a lot of horns. I would say that in a fast game I would be
surprised if you see more than 8 magical tools total, including the
unihorn you keep in your inventory.
3a) A lot of the magical tools that aren't unihorns are really heavy,
the magic horns and harps are all quite heavy. IMO once you're past
the castle a frost horn isn't worth carrying around (vs. a wand of
cold) just for the weight
4) Polypiling for markers always results in a (1:xx) marker

> [...] But we
> definitely have extra wishes to burn if we can use some of them on
> magic markers that *might* give us the spellbook we need -- and if we
> have wishes to burn then we might as well just directly wish for the
> spellbook we need.

5) I think you're really overstating the probability of getting a very
specific spellbook via polypiling. Remember, polypiled spellbooks have
the same probability of getting them in the dungeon. From:
http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/343/spl1-343.txt, We have drain life
being one of the rarest spells in the game, at 10. Sleep, in
comparison, is 50 (on a relative probability scale). I would say
(without doing any math) sleep, detect monsters (43), light (45) are
good spellbooks to get this way, but drain life, identify (20), magic
mapping (18), detect treasure (20), jumping (20) aren't, especially
given the pain in the ass it is to get spellbooks all way from VoD &
the Castle (where there usually are 4-6 or so) back up to your stash
(IME most people like to put it either near an altar close to sokoban,
or in sokoban itself) - unless you have a good way of doing level
teleport consistently. I think I've gotten identify exactly once
polypiling spellbooks, and I don't recall ever getting magic mapping
from polypiling them.

